#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:-1
msgid ""
"Looking to optimize your documentation project for search engines? This SEO "
"guide will help your docs be better understood by both people and crawlers "
"as well as help you rank higher in search engine results."
msgstr "想让你的文档项目在搜索引擎中获得更好排名吗？本 SEO 指南将帮助人和爬虫更好地理解你的文档，并提升你在搜索结果中的排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:2
msgid "How to do search engine optimization (SEO) for documentation projects"
msgstr "如何为文档项目做搜索引擎优化（SEO）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:10
msgid ""
"This article explains how documentation can be optimized to appear in search"
" results, ultimately increasing traffic to your docs."
msgstr "本文讲解如何优化文档以出现在搜索结果中，最终为你的文档带来更多流量。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:13
msgid ""
"While you optimize your docs to make them more friendly for search engine "
"spiders/crawlers, it's important to keep in mind that your ultimate goal is "
"to make your docs more :term:`discoverable <discoverability>` for your "
"users."
msgstr "当你优化文档以使其对搜索引擎爬虫更友好时，请牢记最终目标是让你的文档对用户而言更 :term:`易于发现 <discoverability>` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:17
msgid ""
"By following :ref:`our best practices for SEO <guides/technical-docs-seo-"
"guide:Best practices for documentation SEO>`, you can ensure that when a "
"user types a question into a search engine, they can get the answers from "
"your documentation in the search results."
msgstr ""
"遵循 :ref:`我们的 SEO 最佳实践 <guides/technical-docs-seo-guide:Best practices for "
"documentation SEO>` ，你可以确保用户在搜索引擎中输入问题时，能在搜索结果中从你的文档得到答案。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:23
msgid ""
"This guide isn't meant to be your only resource on SEO, and there's a lot of"
" SEO topics not covered here. For additional reading, please see the "
":ref:`external resources <guides/technical-docs-seo-guide:External "
"resources>` section."
msgstr ""
"本指南不应成为你唯一的 SEO 参考，其中许多 SEO 主题未涉及。更多阅读请见 :ref:`外部资源 <guides/technical-docs-"
"seo-guide:External resources>` 一节。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:30
msgid "SEO basics"
msgstr "SEO 基础"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:32
msgid ""
"Search engines like Google and Bing crawl through the internet following "
"links in an attempt to understand and build an index of what various pages "
"and sites are about. This is called \"crawling\" or \"indexing\". When a "
"person sends a query to a search engine, the search engine evaluates this "
"index using a number of factors and attempts to return the results most "
"likely to answer that person's question."
msgstr ""
"Google 和 Bing "
"等搜索引擎通过跟随链接在互联网上爬取，试图理解并建立各类页面和站点的索引。这称为\"爬取\"或\"索引\"。当有人向搜索引擎发出查询时，搜索引擎会依据若干因素评估该索引，并尝试返回最可能回答该问题的结果。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:40
msgid ""
"How search engines \"rank\" sites based on a person's query is part of their"
" secret sauce. While some search engines publish the basics of their "
"algorithms (see Google's published details on PageRank), few search engines "
"give all of the details in an attempt to prevent users from gaming the "
"rankings with low value content which happens to rank well."
msgstr ""
"搜索引擎如何基于用户查询对站点\"排名\"是它们的秘方所在。虽然有些搜索引擎会公布算法的基本原理（参见 Google 公开的 PageRank "
"细节），但很少有搜索引擎披露全部细节，以防用户用碰巧排名不错的低价值内容来操纵排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:47
msgid ""
"Both `Google <https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/35769>`_ and "
"`Bing <https://www.bing.com/webmaster/help/webmaster-guidelines-30fba23a>`_ "
"publish a set of guidelines to help make sites easier to understand for "
"search engines and rank better. To summarize some of the most important "
"aspects as they apply to technical documentation, your site should:"
msgstr ""
"`Google <https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/35769>`_ 和 `Bing "
"<https://www.bing.com/webmaster/help/webmaster-guidelines-30fba23a>`_ "
"都发布了一组指南，帮助站点更容易被搜索引擎理解并获得更好排名。总结其中与技术文档最相关的重要方面，你的站点应当："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:53
msgid ""
"Use descriptive and accurate titles in the HTML ``<title>`` tag. For Sphinx,"
" the ``<title>`` comes from the first heading on the page."
msgstr "在 HTML ``<title>`` 标签中使用描述性且准确的标题。对 Sphinx 而言，``<title>`` 取自页面首个标题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:55
msgid ""
"Ensure your URLs are descriptive. They are displayed in search results. "
"Sphinx uses the source filename without the file extension as the URL."
msgstr "确保 URL 具有描述性。它们会显示在搜索结果中。Sphinx 使用不带扩展名的源文件名作为 URL。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:57
msgid ""
"Make sure the words your readers would search for to find your site are "
"actually included on your pages."
msgstr "确保读者为找到你站点而会搜索的词语确实出现在你的页面中。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:59
msgid "Avoid low content pages or pages with minimal original content."
msgstr "避免低内容页面或原创内容极少的页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:60
msgid ""
"Avoid tactics that attempt to increase your search engine ranking without "
"actually improving content."
msgstr "避免使用未真正改进内容却试图提升搜索排名的手段。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:62
msgid ""
"Google specifically `warns about automatically generated content`_ although "
"this applies primarily to keyword stuffing and low value content. High "
"quality documentation generated from source code (eg. auto generated API "
"documentation) seems OK."
msgstr ""
"Google 特别 `warns about automatically generated content`_ "
"，不过这主要针对关键词堆砌和低价值内容。从源代码生成的高质量文档（如自动生成的 API 文档）似乎没问题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:69
msgid ""
"While both Google and Bing discuss site performance as an important factor "
"in search result ranking, this guide is not going to discuss it in detail. "
"Most technical documentation that uses Sphinx or Read the Docs generates "
"static HTML and the performance is typically decent relative to most of the "
"internet."
msgstr ""
"虽然 Google 和 Bing 都将站点性能视为搜索排名的的重要因素，本指南不打算详细讨论。使用 Sphinx 或 Read the Docs "
"的大多数技术文档生成静态 HTML，相对互联网大部分站点而言性能通常不错。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:77
msgid "Best practices for documentation SEO"
msgstr "文档 SEO 最佳实践"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:79
msgid ""
"Once a crawler or spider finds your site, it will follow links and redirects"
" in an attempt to find any and all pages on your site. While there are a few"
" ways to guide the search engine in its crawl for example by using a "
":ref:`sitemap <seo_sitemap.xml>` or a :ref:`robots.txt file "
"<seo_robots.txt>` which we'll discuss shortly, the most important thing is "
"making sure the spider can follow links on your site and get to all your "
"pages."
msgstr ""
"一旦爬虫找到你的站点，它会跟随链接和重定向，试图找到你站点上的所有页面。虽然有几种方式可以引导搜索引擎的爬取，例如使用 :ref:`站点地图 "
"<seo_sitemap.xml>` 或 :ref:`robots.txt 文件 <seo_robots.txt>` "
"（稍后讨论），但最重要的是确保爬虫能跟随站点上的链接到达所有页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:89
msgid "Avoid unlinked pages ✅️"
msgstr "避免无链接页面 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:91
msgid ""
"When building your documentation, you should ensure that pages aren't "
"*unlinked*, meaning that no other pages or navigation have a link to them."
msgstr "构建文档时，应确保页面不是*无链接的* ，即没有其他页面或导航链接到它们。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:95
msgid ""
"Search engine crawlers will not discover pages that aren't linked from "
"somewhere else on your site."
msgstr "搜索引擎爬虫不会发现那些站点内其他地方没有链接的页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:101
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:149
msgid "Sphinx"
msgstr "Sphinx"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:103
msgid ""
"Sphinx calls pages that don't have links to them \"orphans\" and will throw "
"a warning while building documentation that contains an orphan unless the "
"warning is silenced with the :ref:`orphan directive <sphinx:metadata>`."
msgstr ""
"Sphinx 把没有链接指向的页面称为\"孤儿\"，构建包含孤儿的文档时会发出警告，除非用 :ref:`orphan 指令 "
"<sphinx:metadata>` 屏蔽该警告。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:107
msgid ""
"We recommend failing your builds whenever Sphinx warns you, using the "
"``fail_on_warnings`` option in :ref:`.readthedocs.yaml <config-"
"file/v2:sphinx>`."
msgstr ""
"我们建议每当 Sphinx 发出警告时就让构建失败，可在 :ref:`.readthedocs.yaml <config-"
"file/v2:sphinx>` 中使用 ``fail_on_warnings`` 选项。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:110
msgid "Here is an example of a warning of an unreferenced page::"
msgstr "以下是未引用页面的警告示例::"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:121
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:162
msgid "MkDocs"
msgstr "MkDocs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:123
msgid ""
"MkDocs automatically includes all ``.md`` files in the main navigation 💯️. "
"This makes sure that all files are discoverable by default, however there "
"are configurations that allow for unlinked files in various ways. If you "
"want to scan your documentation for unreferenced files and images, a plugin "
"like `mkdocs-unused-files`_ does the job."
msgstr ""
"MkDocs 自动将所有 ``.md`` 文件纳入主导航 "
"💯️，确保默认情况下所有文件都可被发现。不过也有多种配置方式允许存在无链接文件。若想扫描文档中未被引用的文件和图片，`mkdocs-unused-"
"files`_ 之类的插件可以胜任。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:134
msgid "Avoid uncrawlable content ✅️"
msgstr "避免无法爬取的内容 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:136
msgid ""
"While typically this isn't a problem with technical documentation, try to "
"avoid content that is \"hidden\" from search engines. This includes content "
"hidden in images or videos which the crawler may not understand. For "
"example, if you do have a video in your docs, make sure the rest of that "
"page describes the content of the video."
msgstr "虽然技术文档通常不存在此问题，但仍应尽量避免对搜索引擎\"隐藏\"的内容，包括隐藏在图片或视频中、爬虫可能无法理解的内容。例如，若文档中确有视频，请确保页面其余部分描述了该视频的内容。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:143
msgid ""
"When using images, make sure to set the image alt text or set a caption on "
"figures."
msgstr "使用图片时，请确保设置图片替代文本，或为图表设置标题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:151
msgid ""
"For Sphinx, the image and figure directives support both alt texts and "
"captions:"
msgstr "在 Sphinx 中，image 和 figure 指令都支持替代文本和标题："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:164
msgid "The Markdown syntax defines an alt text for images:"
msgstr "Markdown 语法为图片定义替代文本："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:170
msgid ""
"Though HTML supports figures and captions, Markdown and MkDocs do not have a"
" built-in feature. Instead, you can use markdown extensions such as `md-in-"
"html`_ to allow the necessary HTML structures for including figures:"
msgstr ""
"虽然 HTML 支持图表和标题，Markdown 和 MkDocs 并无内置功能。你可以改用 `md-in-html`_ 等 Markdown "
"扩展，以支持嵌入图表所需的 HTML 结构："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:188
msgid "Redirects ✅️"
msgstr "重定向 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:190
msgid ""
"Redirects tell search engines when content has moved. For example, if this "
"guide moved from ``guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.html`` to ``guides"
"/sphinx-seo-guide.html``, there will be a time period where search engines "
"will still have the old URL in their index and will still be showing it to "
"users. This is why it is important to update your own links within your docs"
" as well as redirecting. If the hostname moved from docs.readthedocs.io to "
"docs.readthedocs.org, this would be even more important!"
msgstr ""
"重定向告诉搜索引擎内容已迁移。例如，若本指南从 ``guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.html`` 移到 ``guides"
"/sphinx-seo-guide.html`` ，会有一段时间搜索引擎索引中仍保留旧 URL "
"并继续向用户展示。这就是为什么除了重定向之外，更新文档内部的链接也很重要。若主机名从 docs.readthedocs.io 变为 "
"docs.readthedocs.org 就更如此！"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:197
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports a few different kinds of :doc:`user defined redirects"
" </user-defined-redirects>` that should cover all the different cases such "
"as redirecting a certain page for all project versions, or redirecting one "
"version to another."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 支持多种 :doc:`用户自定义重定向 </user-defined-redirects>` "
"，可覆盖各种情形，例如为所有项目版本重定向某个页面，或把一个版本重定向到另一个版本。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:207
msgid "Canonical URLs ✅️"
msgstr "规范 URL ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:209
msgid ""
"Anytime very similar content is hosted at multiple URLs, it is pretty "
"important to set a canonical URL. The canonical URL tells search engines "
"where the original version your documentation is even if you have multiple "
"versions on the internet (for example, incomplete translations or deprecated"
" versions)."
msgstr ""
"当非常相似的内容托管在多个 URL 上时，设置规范 URL 就相当重要。即使你的文档在互联网上有多个版本（如未完成的翻译或已废弃的版本），规范 URL "
"也能告诉搜索引擎哪个是原始版本。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:215
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports :doc:`setting the canonical URL </canonical-urls>` if"
" you are using a :doc:`custom domain </custom-domains>` in your project's "
":menuselection:`Settings --> Domains`."
msgstr ""
"若你在项目 :menuselection:`Settings --> Domains` 中使用 :doc:`自定义域名 </custom-"
"domains>` ，Read the Docs 支持 :doc:`设置规范 URL </canonical-urls>` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:223
msgid "Use a robots.txt file ✅️"
msgstr "使用 robots.txt 文件 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:225
msgid ""
"A ``robots.txt`` file is readable by crawlers and lives at the root of your "
"site (eg. https://docs.readthedocs.com/robots.txt). It tells search engines "
"which pages to crawl or not to crawl and can allow you to control how a "
"search engine crawls your site. For example, you may want to request that "
"search engines :ref:`ignore unsupported versions of your documentation "
"<faq:How can I avoid search results having a deprecated version of my "
"docs?>` while keeping those docs online in case people need them."
msgstr ""
"``robots.txt`` 文件可供爬虫读取，位于站点根目录（如 "
"https://docs.readthedocs.com/robots.txt）。它告诉搜索引擎哪些页面该爬取、哪些不该，并让你控制搜索引擎的爬取方式。例如，你可能希望搜索引擎"
" :ref:`忽略不受支持的文档版本 <faq:How can I avoid search results having a deprecated "
"version of my docs?>` ，同时保留这些文档在线以备用户需要。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:233
msgid ""
"By default, Read the Docs serves a ``robots.txt`` for you. To customize this"
" file, you can create a ``robots.txt`` file that is written to your "
"documentation root on your default branch/version."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，Read the Docs 会为你提供 ``robots.txt`` 。要自定义该文件，可创建一个写入默认分支/版本文档根目录的 "
"``robots.txt`` 文件。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:237
msgid ""
"See the `Google's documentation on robots.txt "
"<https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/6062608>`_ for additional "
"details."
msgstr ""
"更多细节见 `Google 关于 robots.txt 的文档 "
"<https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/6062608>`_ 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:243
msgid "Use a sitemap.xml file ✅️"
msgstr "使用 sitemap.xml 文件 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:245
msgid ""
"A sitemap is a file readable by crawlers that contains a list of pages and "
"other files on your site and some metadata or relationships about them (eg. "
"https://docs.readthedocs.com/sitemap.xml). A good sitemaps provides "
"information like how frequently a page or file is updated or any alternate "
"language versions of a page."
msgstr ""
"站点地图是供爬虫读取的文件，包含站点上页面和其他文件的列表及其元数据或关系（如 "
"https://docs.readthedocs.com/sitemap.xml）。一份好的站点地图会提供诸如页面或文件的更新频率、页面的其他语言版本等信息。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:251
msgid ""
"Read the Docs generates a sitemap for you that contains the last time your "
"documentation was updated as well as links to active versions, subprojects, "
"and translations your project has. We have a small separate guide on "
":doc:`sitemaps </reference/sitemaps>`."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 会为你生成站点地图，其中包含文档最后更新时间，以及指向项目活跃版本、子项目和翻译的链接。我们另有一篇简短的 "
":doc:`站点地图 </reference/sitemaps>` 指南。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:255
msgid ""
"See the `Google docs on building a sitemap "
"<https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/183668>`_."
msgstr ""
"参见 `Google 关于构建站点地图的文档 "
"<https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/183668>`_ 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:259
msgid "Use meta tags ✅️"
msgstr "使用 meta 标签 ✅️"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:261
msgid ""
"Using a meta description allows you to customize how your pages look in "
"search engine result pages."
msgstr "使用 meta description 可让你自定义页面在搜索结果页中的显示方式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:264
msgid ""
"Typically search engines will use the first few sentences of a page if no "
"meta description is provided. In Sphinx, you can customize your meta "
"description using the following RestructuredText:"
msgstr ""
"通常未提供 meta description 时，搜索引擎会使用页面开头几句。在 Sphinx 中，可用以下 reStructuredText 自定义 "
"meta description："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:279
msgid "Google search engine results showing a customized meta description"
msgstr "显示自定义 meta description 的 Google 搜索结果"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:281
msgid ""
"Moz.com, an authority on search engine optimization, makes the following "
"suggestions for meta descriptions:"
msgstr "搜索引擎优化权威站点 Moz.com 对 meta description 提出以下建议："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:284
msgid ""
"Your meta description should have the most relevant content of the page. A "
"searcher should know whether they've found the right page from the "
"description."
msgstr "你的 meta description 应包含页面中最相关的内容。搜索者应能从中判断是否找到了正确的页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:286
msgid ""
"The meta description should be between 150-300 characters and it may be "
"truncated down to around 150 characters in some situations."
msgstr "meta description 应在 150–300 字符之间，在某些情况下可能被截断到约 150 字符。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:288
msgid "Meta descriptions are used for display but not for ranking."
msgstr "meta description 用于展示，不用于排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:290
msgid ""
"Search engines don't always use your customized meta description if they "
"think a snippet from the page is a better description."
msgstr "若搜索引擎认为页面中的片段是更好的描述，它们不一定会使用你自定义的 meta description。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:294
msgid "Measure, iterate, & improve"
msgstr "度量、迭代与改进"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:296
msgid ""
"Search engines (and soon, Read the Docs itself) can provide useful data that"
" you can use to improve your docs' ranking on search engines."
msgstr "搜索引擎（以及不久后的 Read the Docs 自身）能提供有用数据，帮助你改善文档在搜索引擎中的排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:301
msgid "Search engine feedback"
msgstr "搜索引擎反馈"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:303
msgid ""
"`Google Search Console <https://search.google.com/search-console>`_ and "
"`Bing Webmaster Tools <https://www.bing.com/webmaster/help/webmaster-"
"guidelines-30fba23a>`_ are tools for webmasters to get feedback about the "
"crawling of their sites (or docs in our case). Some of the most valuable "
"feedback these provide include:"
msgstr ""
"`Google Search Console <https://search.google.com/search-console>`_ 和 `Bing "
"Webmaster Tools <https://www.bing.com/webmaster/help/webmaster-guidelines-"
"30fba23a>`_ 是供站长了解站点（在我们的场景下即文档）爬取情况的工具。它们提供的最有价值的反馈包括："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:309
msgid ""
"Google and Bing will show pages that were previously indexed that now give a"
" 404 (or more rarely a 500 or other status code). These will remain in the "
"index for some time but will eventually be removed. This is a good "
"opportunity to create a :ref:`redirect <seo_redirects>`."
msgstr ""
"Google 和 Bing 会显示此前已被索引、现在返回 404（或更少见地返回 500 "
"等其他状态码）的页面。这些页面会在索引中保留一段时间，最终被移除。此时正是创建 :ref:`重定向 <seo_redirects>` 的好时机。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:313
msgid "These tools will show any crawl issues with your documentation."
msgstr "这些工具会显示你的文档中的爬取问题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:314
msgid ""
"Search Console and Webmaster Tools will highlight security issues found or "
"if Google or Bing took action against your site because they believe it is "
"spammy."
msgstr ""
"Search Console 和 Webmaster Tools 会突出显示发现的安全问题，或 Google、Bing "
"因认为你的站点含垃圾内容而对其采取的措施。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:319
msgid "Analytics tools"
msgstr "分析工具"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:321
msgid ""
"A tool like Google Analytics, along with our :doc:`integrated Read the Docs "
"analytics </traffic-analytics>`, can give you feedback about the search "
"terms people use to find your docs, your most popular pages, and lots of "
"other useful data."
msgstr ""
"Google Analytics 之类的工具，加上我们 :doc:`集成的 Read the Docs 分析 </traffic-analytics>`"
" ，能给你关于人们用来找到你文档的搜索词、最受欢迎页面以及大量其他有用数据的反馈。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:326
msgid ""
"Search term feedback can be used to help you optimize content for certain "
"keywords or for related keywords. For Sphinx documentation, or other "
"technical documentation that has its own search features, analytics tools "
"can also tell you the terms people search for within your site."
msgstr "搜索词反馈可帮助你针对特定关键词或相关关键词优化内容。对 Sphinx 文档或其他自带搜索功能的技术文档，分析工具还能告诉你用户在站点内搜索的词。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide.rst:330
msgid ""
"Knowing your popular pages can help you prioritize where to spend your SEO "
"efforts. Optimizing your already popular pages can have a significant "
"impact."
msgstr "了解哪些页面受欢迎，可帮助你确定 SEO 投入的优先顺序。优化已受欢迎的页面能带来显著影响。"

